---
description: |
  Detects the SOC Prime High-Order Sigma rule "APT Malware Attack Cases by the
  Kimsuky Group Impersonating Diplomats".

  The Kimsuky group is conducting spear phishing campaigns by impersonating
  diplomatic personnel to target the education sector. The attacks utilize LNK
  files and PowerShell scripts to deploy a variety of malware including the
  PebbleDash backdoor, PrxClient proxy and RDP Wrapper. These tools are used
  for remote control, privilege escalation and data exfiltration.

  The rule chains 3 stages of SOC Prime behavior rules by host. See
  `socprime::hos::chain` for the correlation and the resulting Detection
  Finding.
args:
  named:
    - name: timeframe
      type: duration
      default: 30min
      description: The time span that a chain must fit into.
    - name: threshold
      type: float
      default: 0.6
      description: The share of stages a host must cover, between 0 and 1.
    - name: tolerance
      type: duration
      default: 1min
      description: How far findings of a host may arrive out of time order.
---

// Generated by scripts/vendor.py from the SOC Prime HoS rule r0LqNjnpT21W.
let $stages = {
  seq1: [
    "6c5038d3-6675-4686-a15b-d9780b21a7cc", // Possible Malicious LNK File with Double Extension (via cmdline)
    "7c01d1e4-89de-476f-a996-eb768978994a", // The Possibility of Execution Through Hidden PowerShell Command Lines (via cmdline)
    "309111d8-89ad-4c98-a799-10053a40bd0a", // Suspicious Powershell Strings (via powershell)
  ],
  seq2: [
    "c4d9d7cc-6f1e-45ae-bd7b-0c83e8029fef", // Suspicious Files in Public User Profile (via file_event)
    "44daab1f-109a-4c20-9f64-5401c1a9ab47", // Suspicious Execution from Public User Profile (via process_creation)
    "bc139ef2-0c05-4cf7-b7af-3261d2cb2d68", // LOLBAS WScript / CScript (via process_creation)
    "63f2ae8a-6912-4ea9-ad2c-369f4555a549", // Suspicious Windows DNS Query by Windows Script Host [wscript.exe] (via dns_query)
  ],
  seq3: [
    "4ab60adc-7117-4f20-80de-77ecf2a1ef99", // Call Suspicious .NET Methods from Powershell (via powershell)
    "ecedd60a-3de3-420c-adc5-f35bd3871365", // System Processes Execution from Untypical Paths (via process_creation)
    "8a701e5f-a0a6-4f58-9a35-1f29a08e4f79", // Possible Account or Group Enumeration / Manipulation (via cmdline)
    "0c5583a2-c83a-4c56-9304-f7c394cbbada", // Possible Remote Desktop Services Shadowing (via process_creation)
    "a5cdc145-e4d3-4b0f-8a56-ddc2850f3cdf", // UserAccount Hidden via Registry (via registry_event)
  ],
}
sigma rules=[...$stages.seq1, ...$stages.seq2, ...$stages.seq3].map(uid => socprime::$rules[uid])
socprime::hos::chain uid="bc64829a-a6c0-44ec-aa9a-2ffc5b773dfe",
  name="APT Malware Attack Cases by the Kimsuky Group Impersonating Diplomats",
  level="high",
  tags=[],
  stages=$stages,
  timeframe=$timeframe,
  threshold=$threshold,
  tolerance=$tolerance
